    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104-a1">

                <pb facs="0268" n="196" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg196"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 305.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Granville to Mr.
                            Lowell</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1882-02-02"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 2,
                        1882</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my letter of the 30th of
                    December last, I have been informed by Her Majesty’s secretary of state for the
                    home department that he did not fail to refer to the lord lieutenant of Ireland
                    your communication on the subject of Denis Hayes O’Connor, now in custody under
                    the protection of person and property (Ireland) act, 1881, but that his
                    excellency has expressed his regret that he cannot, consistently with his duty,
                    order the prisoner’s release at present.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>GRANVILLE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
